---
const isLatest = import.meta.env.NOVELTEA_DOCS_RENDER_CHANNEL === 'latest';
const releaseVersion = import.meta.env.NOVELTEA_DOCS_RELEASE_VERSION?.trim();
const docsRoot = isLatest ? '/docs' : '/docs/dev';
---

{isLatest ? (
  <p>
    These docs describe the latest public NovelTea release{releaseVersion ? ` (${releaseVersion})` : ''}.
    They are rendered from that release's exact source revision so hand-authored guidance and generated
    reference stay aligned with the released tooling.
  </p>
) : (
  <aside class="docs-development-notice">
    <strong>Unreleased development channel.</strong> These docs describe current NovelTea development
    behavior and may change before a public release.
  </aside>
)}

<p>
  NovelTea is a narrative-game engine and editor built around portable project data, a native runtime,
  Lua scripting, and export targets including desktop and Web.
</p>

<h2>What belongs here</h2>

<p>
  The public documentation focuses on authors using NovelTea rather than the engine's internal
  implementation. As the surface stabilizes, this section will grow to cover project structure, rooms
  and interactions, UI authoring, scripting, validation, preview, and export workflows.
</p>

<h2>Channel status</h2>

<p>
  {isLatest
    ? 'This is the Latest channel. Use Dev when you intentionally want documentation for current master development.'
    : 'This is the Dev channel and tracks current master development rather than a compatibility promise.'}
</p>

<h2>Next places to visit</h2>

<ul>
  <li><a href={`${docsRoot}/reference/`}>Project schema reference</a> — generated human-readable Project Workspace and record reference with raw schemas available for exact constraints.</li>
  <li><a href="/examples/">Examples</a> — the latest public release, or the development channel before the first release.</li>
  <li><a href="/download/">Downloads</a> — current public-build availability and editor/CLI downloads.</li>
</ul>

<style>
  .docs-development-notice {
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    background: var(--sl-color-bg-inline-code);
  }
</style>
